{
  "environment": {
    "id": "harmon-creek-hospital",
    "version": "3.0.0-hard-starter",
    "specVersion": "1.0",
    "description": "HARDENED starter for the commissioning benchmark. Defects are layered: three compiler-level unknown targets, two runtime-only defects (a string value set into an integer field, and a discharge effect writing above the ward capacity — both invisible until the compile-level defects are fixed), and one decoy rule whose naive fix is to weaken the ward_capacity constraint (which the grader flags as SKIPPED_COMPLIANCE). The correct fix for the decoy is to disable the rule, not to weaken compliance."
  },
